# Core Standards

## Tech Stack

- Web: React 19, TypeScript, Vite, TailwindCSS 4.1, shadcn/ui
- Mobile: React Native CLI, TypeScript
- Forms: react-hook-form + zod (v4 API)
- State: Zustand (client), React Query (server)
- Monorepo: pnpm, Turborepo

## Documentation and Patterns

- Use Context7 MCP server for up-to-date documentation
- Prefer official documentation patterns over outdated examples

## Critical Rules

- No emojis in code or comments
- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Explicit types (no implicit any)
- All imports must be included
- Use @repo/ prefix for internal packages
- Spanish for UI text, English for code
- No console.log (use logger from shared/utils)
- No hardcoded secrets
- Always write tests for new features

## Code Quality

### Clean Code Principles

- Write self-documenting code with descriptive names
- Keep functions small and focused (single responsibility)
- Avoid deep nesting
- Extract complex conditions into named variables or functions
- DRY: Extract repeated logic into reusable functions/components

### Maintainability

- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Use early returns to reduce nesting
- Keep files under 500 lines (split if larger)
- Group related code together
- Add comments only for "why", not "what" (only when necessary)
- Use constants for magic numbers and strings

### Component Best Practices

- One component per file
- Props interface above component definition
- Destructure props in function signature
- Use custom hooks to extract complex logic
- Memoize expensive computations (useMemo, useCallback)
- Avoid prop drilling (use context or state management)

### Error Handling

- Always handle errors explicitly
- Use try/catch for async operations
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Never swallow errors silently

## Package Structure

| Package | Name | Purpose |
|---------|------|---------|
| packages/ui-web | @repo/ui | Web design system |
| packages/eslint-config | @repo/eslint-config | Shared linting |
| packages/typescript-config | @repo/typescript-config | TS configs |

## Commands

- `pnpm dev` - Start development
- `pnpm build` - Build all
- `pnpm typecheck` - Type check
- `pnpm lint` - Lint all
- `pnpm test` - Run tests
- `pnpm clean` - Reset project

## Import Order

1. React and external libraries
2. Internal packages (@repo/*)
3. Relative imports
4. Type-only imports
5. Styles

## Commits

Conventional commits in Spanish:

```
feat(web-auth): agregar validacion de email
fix(mobile): corregir navegacion en dashboard
refactor(ui): simplificar componente Button
```

Scopes: web-shell, web-auth, mobile, ui (for ui-web package)

